Global reserves of lithium, cobalt, and rare earth elements are finite; recycling batteries and electronics is increasingly critical to securing supply chains for clean energy technologies.
The circular economy model (designing products for recycling) is estimated to generate €1.8 trillion in economic value for Europe by 2030, by keeping materials in use rather than requiring virgin extraction.
Copper recycling meets 35% of global demand and growing — given copper's role in electrification and renewables, this recycled fraction is an essential resource security measure.
